# General Guidelines

- Always answer questions directly first
- Use actual workspace paths in docs and examples; do not use placeholder paths
- Never make code changes without an explicit user request
- Comment and documentation rules live in `documentation-standards.mdc`
- Java style lives in `java-standards.mdc`

## Classroom

- Students do **not** author this code. The teacher updates robots and simulations at classtime from their suggestions
- Keep every change explainable on a projector in one sitting
- Prefer the smallest edit that demonstrates the student's idea
- Do not "improve" a strategy with advanced Java or extra tactics unless asked

## Maven Layout

- `/Volumes/Projects/RoboBattle/pom.xml` — aggregator; JDK **21** via `maven.compiler.source` / `maven.compiler.target`
- `/Volumes/Projects/RoboBattle/robots/` — agents and support classes reused by every simulation (`com.dietzmoss.robots`)
- `/Volumes/Projects/RoboBattle/simulations/` — runnable simulation apps (`com.dietzmoss.simulations`); depends on `robots`

Each simulation is started from a matching IDE Run configuration or `robo-battle <name>`.

Do not add toolchain, wrapper, or extra JDK pinning unless asked. The parent POM already targets 21.

## Formatting

- 4-space indent, UTF-8, final newline, trim trailing whitespace
- Opening braces on their own line (Allman)
